# Third-party packages. The workspace root grows a node_modules/ from wrangler
# and vitest runs, and it was never ignored here (only the sub-repos ignore it),
# so a broad `git add` swept two cache files into history on 2026-07-28 —
# including a wrangler account-id cache. Regenerated on demand; never committed.
node_modules/

# Cloned repos (managed by setup.sh)
youcoded/
youcoded-core/
youcoded-admin/
wecoded-themes/
wecoded-marketplace/

# Worktrees and temp directories
.worktrees/
*-worktree*/
*-unified/
*-phase*/
*-decoupling/
*-sessions/

# Skill runtime state (brainstorming/writing-plans session dirs etc).
# Contain ephemeral working notes from skill invocations and don't carry
# value across machines.
.superpowers/

# Ad-hoc scratch dir occasionally used for files we don't want to track.
# If something proves useful, promote it to scripts/ or docs/.
scratch/

# Auto-title artifacts
.auto-title
.auto-title-audit.tmp

# Claude project config
# Track: commands/, hooks/, rules/, skills/, settings.json (shared across machines)
# Ignore: settings.local.json (user/machine-specific), worktrees/
.claude/*
!.claude/commands/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/rules/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/settings.json
.youcoded/

# Worktree container dirs (per-repo .wt convention)
*.wt/
scratch-*/
# The workspace-level worktree container (CLAUDE.md convention: worktrees/<name>).
# Each entry is its own git checkout — committing them embeds foreign repos.
worktrees/
# Downloaded release/beta installers used for VM install testing — large
# binaries that must never enter git history.
beta/

# Full event-stream transcripts from the harness review runner
# (youcoded/desktop/test-engine/review-harness.mjs). A transcript is a
# debugging artifact for the session that produced it, not durable history —
# five models' full event streams would dominate this repo's diff history.
# The reviews themselves (appended into the investigation doc) are the
# durable record.
docs/active/investigations/harness-review-runs/
docs/active/investigations/conversation-triage-runs/
